{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784372961,"nonce":"sDdUxDdvESrtxTYl9LLXTFuVnio=","title":"web-ui(dashboard): rework run bar chart — height = run duration, rounded, refined","message":"The dashboard pass/fail strip (RunBars) reads flat and ugly: every bar is full height, so it carries only pass/fail, not how long each run took. Encode run DURATION in bar height (RunSummaryDto gains duration_ms = updated_at - created_at, threaded through RunSummary + Postgres + testkit + list_runs/list_repo_runs). Redesign the bars: rounded tops, a min-height floor so short runs stay visible, a sensible (sqrt/log) height scale so one long run doesn't flatten the rest, better spacing/color. Regen openapi + client.","files":null}]}